# CHANGELOG.md only ever grows: every change appends an entry to a section, and
# nobody rewrites someone else's line. Two branches adding an entry to the same
# section therefore conflict on every rebase, even though the two entries are
# independent and both must be kept.
#
# `merge=union` keeps both sides instead of raising a conflict. It is the right
# driver precisely because entries are append-only and independent — if two
# branches ever do edit the same line, union keeps both copies, which is visible
# in review rather than silent.
#
# Placement conventions do not solve this: whether entries go at the top or the
# bottom of a section, concurrent additions still land on the same line.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
